      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/royal_iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Eliza Nelson, the town's first postmaster, chose the name 'Royal' for the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/royal_iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Royal grew alongside the expansion of railroads across northwest Iowa, which helped farmers ship grain and livestock to larger markets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/royal_iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town sits on soils from the Des Moines Lobe, once prairie but now largely farmland.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/royal_iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "During the 1930s Dust Bowl, Royal’s surrounding farms suffered severe drought and soil erosion.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/royal_iowa"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Royal lies in Clay County, in northwestern Iowa, within the Lakes and Land region.",
